"""Write bounded physical verdicts after raw and independent evidence review."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv
import json

B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT=B.parent
CASES={
'Q001':('REFUTED','The S74 BTJD 3326.9 trough is a gap-associated step shared with Q007. S75 and S82 selected minima have broad baseline-discontinuity shapes, and local trapezoids reach their width bounds. No repeated isolated eclipse morphology is established.','This refutes the selected bulk flags as evidence for this target, not any other possible binary signal.','Seek an isolated full target-centered event before revisiting an eclipse claim.'),
'Q002':('PLAUSIBLE','Several shallow S3 minima and short S30/S97 features are present in raw SAP at about 1-2 ppt, embedded in similar-amplitude short-timescale variability. The S3 BTJD 1404.5 and S30 BTJD 2120.1 features happen to lie near twelve Gaia-period cycles, but the S3 center is not a measured eclipse center and the shapes do not establish same-kind recurrence. The projected S97 BTJD 3968.21 window has many quality-zero cadences yet a 0.308-d left-baseline gap and similar intrinsic modulation, so it is not a sensitive exclusion.','The eclipse interpretation, clock and target-specific geometry remain insecure. KSPSAP strongly suppresses several S3 minima on the same photons, which alone cannot refute raw variability.','Acquire a distinct source-centered eclipse with stable morphology and a measured clock; test actual aliases and capable neighbors.'),
'Q003':('REFUTED','S94 BTJD 3874.9 and S104 BTJD 4197.0 reproduce the detailed asymmetric dip, partial recovery and gap-locked rise seen in other queued stars. Their apparent recurrence is shared detector structure, not an isolated source-specific eclipse.','The selected-window verdict does not rule out unrelated eclipses elsewhere in this star.','Require an isolated full event with valid target pixels.'),
'Q004':('REFUTED','The S94 BTJD 3874.9 dip is the same detailed shared gap-linked waveform as Q003/Q006/Q008. The S101 BTJD 4111.9 selection follows a baseline step/gap trend and does not reproduce a discrete eclipse.','No secure same-kind raw centers or orbit association result from these selected windows.','Find and localize an isolated repeated dip.'),
'Q005':('PLAUSIBLE','Three broad raw troughs in S5, S32 and S98 near BTJD 1455.8, 2194.2 and 4039.5 have similar steep-drop, partial-rebound, second-low morphology. Their broad centers are compatible with sixteen and forty cycles of Gaia P=46.13747 d. Fresh target-vicinity apertures reproduce the S32 trough and an additional S98 feature near BTJD 4016.6, the Gaia P/2 phase from S32. The latter is a substantial pixel-level feature, not a clean subharmonic null, but its shape differs from 4039.5 and could be opposite-kind variation or orbital modulation. The troughs support recurring photometric variation, yet their double structure and asymmetric trends are not discrete eclipse morphology.','Broad center estimates and widths do not establish a unique same-kind clock. Orbital/periastron modulation and baseline effects remain alternatives. A brighter source about five pixels away and unresolved close neighbors limit ownership; S98 background varies sharply. Same-photon KSPSAP suppression is not an independent physical refutation.','Obtain a clean full event with source-resolved pixels and test aliases and Gaia conjunction geometry.'),
'Q006':('REFUTED','Many 1-ppt flagged minima in S9/S10/S13/S34/S36/S87/S88 resemble short-timescale quasi-periodic variability rather than a repeated discrete eclipse. The larger S94 BTJD 3874.9 flag shares the exact gap-linked common waveform of Q003/Q004/Q008; S97 flags are broad baseline structures.','This concerns the selected eclipse interpretation; the star remains variable and could have other unexamined binary signals.','Measure a stable source-specific eclipse waveform in independent observing windows before assigning a clock.'),
'Q007':('REFUTED','The S74 BTJD 3326.9 trough shares a gap-associated step/recovery with Q001. Both S80 flags are broad baseline trends with bound-hitting local fits rather than discrete repeat eclipses.','The selected flags do not establish an eclipse sequence; other variability remains possible.','Inspect an isolated raw dip in another sector with valid target pixels.'),
'Q008':('REFUTED','S94 BTJD 3874.9 and S104 BTJD 4197.3 share the same detailed gap-linked S94/S104 waveform as Q003, with broad bound-hitting fits and no isolated eclipse core.','The apparent cross-sector repetition is instrumental evidence for the selected windows only.','Require an isolated target-centered full eclipse to reopen.'),
'Q009':('PLAUSIBLE','S95 BTJD 3894.5 and S96 BTJD 3921.7 show sharp raw changes immediately beside roughly 1.3-d gaps. The core/wing coverage is incomplete and local fits are singular or boundary-limited; neither event is a secure measured eclipse center. Two selected sectors alone do not demonstrate same-kind recurrence.','Gap-edge systematics are a credible alternative but the available evidence does not positively refute a real eclipse. No period or depth is adopted.','Catch a complete isolated event with both baselines and valid source-resolved pixels.'),
'Q010':('REFUTED','The S104 BTJD 4197.5 broad trough shares the Q003/Q008 common-mode shape, and its fresh difference image has a positive/negative dipole consistent with motion. S96 minima near BTJD 3919.8 and 3926.3 are gap/baseline trends with width-bound fits rather than a stable eclipse sequence.','The selected windows do not establish a source-specific eclipse; any independent variability remains unclassified.','Find a clean full target-centered event before adopting timing.'),
}

fields=['sample_id','tic','sample_stratum','physical_verdict','full_review_completion','novelty_status','period_days','period_error_days','primary_epoch_btjd','depth_ppt','limitations','next_check','report']
results=[]
for row in csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(encoding='utf8',newline='')):
    sid=row['sample_id']; tic=row['tic']; verdict,finding,limits,next_check=CASES[sid]
    packet=json.loads((ROOT/'source-packets'/tic/'sources.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
    meas=json.loads((B/tic/'lead-measurements.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
    events=', '.join(f"S{x['sector']} {x['screen_center_btjd']:.3f}" for x in meas['screen_flagged_dips'])
    report=(B/tic/'REPORT.md').resolve()
    lines=[f'# {sid} / TIC {tic}', '',f'**Physical verdict:** {verdict}; **bounded review:** COMPLETE; **catalogue status:** UNKNOWN.','',
           '## Raw evidence','',finding,'',f'Selected screen windows: {events}. These are detector predictions, not adopted eclipse centers. Lead numeric and original source receipts: `lead-measurements.json`; raw plots: `lead-event-panels.png`; same-photon QLP reduction: `lead-alternative.json`. Independent visual and TESSCut checks: `../helper-audit.md` and helper-prefixed artifacts.','',
           '## Timing, identity and limits','',f'Frozen Gaia DR3 source {row["gaia_dr3"]}; selection spectroscopic period {float(row["gaia_period_days"]):.6f} d. This is an orbital prior, not a photometric clock or source-specific conjunction match.','',
           'Novelty remains UNKNOWN: the queue-wide catalogue audit has no successful fresh VSX/ASAS-SN/Kostov gate for this target; a failed query is not a nonmatch. Physical classification is independent of novelty.','',limits,'',
           'No unsupported photometric period, precision error, primary epoch or depth is adopted. Same-photon reductions are processing comparisons, not independent observing occasions. This bounded verdict concerns the selected bulk lead, not every possible signal from this star.','',
           '## Next check','',next_check,'']
    if sid=='Q002': lines+=['Actual projected S97 coverage and baseline limitation: `../helper-Q002-null.json`.','']
    if sid=='Q005': lines+=['Gaia-projected windows and actual cadence coverage: `../helper-Q005-predictions.json`; conditional subharmonic windows: `lead-q005-alias-windows.json`. The S98 4016.6 half-period feature and valid target-vicinity aperture are documented in `../helper-Q005-s98-alias.json` and `../helper-Q005-s98-diff.json`, with cutout receipt in `../helper-cut-receipts.json`. These do not prove an orbital eclipse or unique same-kind cycle.','']
    report.write_text('\n'.join(lines),encoding='utf8')
    results.append(dict(sample_id=sid,tic=tic,sample_stratum=row['sample_stratum'],physical_verdict=verdict,full_review_completion='COMPLETE',novelty_status='UNKNOWN',period_days='',period_error_days='',primary_epoch_btjd='',depth_ppt='',limitations=limits,next_check=next_check,report=str(report)))
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',encoding='utf8',newline='') as f:
    writer=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields); writer.writeheader(); writer.writerows(results)
print([(r['sample_id'],r['physical_verdict']) for r in results])
